          ],
          "basis": [
            "E1"
          ],
          "reason": "E1 (accepted delivery_readiness receipt, ready=false, public test passed) records the work_root package as missing both complete_current_code_or_evidence and independent_current_review, and the package is completed=false. The probed obligation work_root/independent_review is UNSATISFIED with no fresh receipt while BLOCKED on work_root/complete_package; that upstream delivery obligation remains owed even though the review must come first in sequence. work_root/complete_package is UNSATISFIED and READY, so the worker's first action is to complete the package (produce current code/evidence), which is the distinct product that unblocks the review. fix_tree and submit are UNKNOWN workflow successors with no evidenced debt and are excluded. Route K adds no organizational change ('none' added product) and no patch is needed; D1 would add an assignment with no distinct product, so it is not chosen. No sustained repair failure, stall, or conflict is evidenced (A4 verification-only candidate is not established because the block is a dependency, not a failed check), so the anomaly is dependency A2.",
          "reconsider_after": "A fresh receipt for work_root/complete_package (current code/evidence accepted) appears, or E1 is superseded such that work_root/independent_review becomes READY and its completion must be re-probed.",
          "anomaly": "A2",
          "probe_completion": "UNSATISFIED",
          "probe_readiness": "BLOCKED"
        },
